Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs: needs-research issues are research, not code -
 break them down first

The needs-research label marks a large idea with open questions. It is
not picked for code: its work is answering the questions in comments and
filing concrete sub-issues (each with P*, area:*, Done means, Part of #N),
then closing the umbrella. README's Issues section explains it to
contributors; AGENTS.md's Pick query excludes it and a new Issue Law
bullet says how agents work one (user, 2026-11-08).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
